  "body_mappings": [
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        498.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        597.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "Dolly was born at Roslin, Scotland, on 5 July 1996. Her genome came from a Finn Dorset ewe's mammary cell, fused with a Blackface egg stripped of its nucleus. A Blackface surrogate carried the embryo through pregnancy, yet her white face was proof of a genetically different lineage. She alone survived from 277 attempts, an extraordinary failure rate."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        391.1614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        490.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "Dolly is popularly called the first clone, a misconception. Her predecessors included frogs cloned from transplanted nuclei in 1962 and Roslin's embryo-derived duo, Megan and Morag, in 1995. She was genuinely the first mammal cloned from an adult cell. Roslin's announcement on 22 February 1997 coincided with the paper, and her name, a mammary pun, honoured Dolly Parton."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        303.46141732283473,
        461.8976377952756,
        382.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "The news provoked uproar and apprehension about the ethics of human cloning. In March 1997 Clinton prohibited federal funding for such experiments. In 1999 her telomeres, or chromosome tips, were reported shortened by about 20% for her age. That fed anxiety; some speculated she was ageing prematurely."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        195.96141732283473,
        461.8976377952756,
        294.96141732283473
      ],
      "text": "Dolly was put down, aged six, on 14 February 2003, with arthritis and a progressive lung disease caused by a sheep virus. Indoor confinement probably contributed. In July 2016, 13 clones, four from her cell line, were ageing normally, without hypertension or diabetes. In November 2017, her skeletal X-rays showed ordinary arthritis, and fears of early onset were judged unfounded."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        108.26141732283473,
        461.8976377952756,
        187.46141732283473
      ],
      "text": "She bore six lambs by natural mating; Bonnie, first of these descendants, arrived in April 1998. Since 2003 her stuffed body, now famously an icon and memorial, has been encased in the National Museum of Scotland. Behind glass, her white face plainly testifies to her Finn Dorset ancestry."
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        517.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        597.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "1996年7月5日，多莉在苏格兰罗斯林出生。她的基因组来自一只芬兰多塞特母羊的乳腺细胞，这个细胞融合了一枚黑脸羊卵细胞，这枚卵已去除了细胞核。一只黑脸羊代孕母羊怀着这个胚胎度过了孕期，而多莉的白脸则是一个基因上不同血统的证明。只有她从277次尝试中存活了下来，一个异乎寻常的失败率。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        409.1614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        509.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "多莉一般被称为第一个克隆体，这是一个错误的观念。她的前几代包括于1962年由移植的细胞核克隆出的青蛙，以及罗斯林于1995年由胚胎衍生的一对绵羊：梅根和莫拉格。她确实是第一个用成年细胞克隆出的哺乳动物。1997年2月22日罗斯林的公告与这篇论文同时发生，而她的名字，一个关于乳腺的双关语，致敬了多莉·帕顿。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        340.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        400.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "这一消息引发了轩然大波，以及关于人类克隆伦理的忧虑。1997年3月，克林顿禁止联邦资金用于这类实验。1999年，她的端粒，即染色体末端，据报道比同龄羊缩短了约20%。这加剧了人们的焦虑；有人推测她正在过早衰老。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        232.16141732283472,
        461.8976377952756,
        332.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "多莉被实施安乐死，时年六岁，那是2003年2月14日；她患有关节炎和一种进行性的肺部疾病，引起它的是绵羊病毒。被限制在室内很可能是原因之一。2016年7月，13只克隆羊，其中4只来自与她相同的细胞系，正在正常衰老，没有高血压，也没有糖尿病。2017年11月，她的骨骼X光片显示出寻常的关节炎，而对提前发病的担忧被判定为毫无根据。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        143.66141732283472,
        461.8976377952756,
        223.66141732283472
      ],
      "text": "她产下六只小羊，是通过自然交配；邦妮是这些后代中的第一只，生于1998年4月。自2003年起，她的填充标本，如今已成为出了名的标志和纪念物，一直封存在苏格兰国家博物馆。隔着玻璃，她的白脸清楚地证明着她的芬兰多塞特祖源。"
    }
  ],
